    "| 2026-11-03 | Cell 2 statistics rebuilt from what the CSV showed: (1) forecast elevations +0.082 m datum fix; (2) all `ss_` statistics from the `TWL` elevation series, with exact-zero placeholders removed; (3) `ss_twl_2pct_peaks` is now an elevation computed here from runup maxima (Shorescan's file value, which is a height above `twl_tide`, is kept as `ss_twl_2pct_peaks_file` converted to elevation); (4) new `ss_R2` and `ss_setup` above forecast tide + surge (`cc_swl`); (5) Shorescan's spectral swash and periods saved; (6) all forecast terms saved; (7) `clipped` flag, `t_mid_utc`, QC counts. Removed `ss_ru_2pct`, `ss_zrunup_mean`, `ss_zrunup_std` (heights above the old, datum-shifted tide that includes setup). `beta06` is no longer required to keep a row. Cell 3 plots the 2% elevation, not the mean. |\n",
    "| 2026-11-03 | Section 4 (threshold cells) updated: reads the combined CSV from cell 2 via `RUN_TAG`; intervals paired without a loop; bursts labelled by UTC time with a vectorised in-interval test (replaces a cross-join and a text comparison of mixed-offset times); `THRESH_TZ` setting for the threshold file; plots the 2% runup elevation (not the mean) with clipped bursts removed; bias/RMSE per interval; plot saved to `plot_dir`. |\n",
    "| 2026-11-03 | TWL comparison plots (Sections 3 and 4) show n, r, R², bias, RMSE and the fitted line per camera / interval and overall, from one shared `fit_stats` helper; the same table is printed. |\n",
    "| 2026-11-03 | Section 4 intervals paired by survey and threshold (not row order); crossings not reached within 21 days set to the window edge; nested intervals labelled with the smallest threshold; threshold times confirmed as UTC (NDBC reports UTC only; `waveDataDownloader.ipynb` does not convert). |\n",
