    "## 1. Transect elevations for one burst\n",
    "Plots `elevation_transect` against `localX_transect` for each transect of a single burst: the raw profile dotted, the\n",
    "cleaned profile solid, and removed spikes as crosses (see *Profile cleaning* above). Use it to check the profiles\n",
    "behind the problems in Section 2b, e.g. a flat stretch near 2.1–2.2 m on transect 20 or a profile ending near 1.35 m on\n",
    "transect 70.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Finding the files.** Files are matched with the same `STACK_RE` pattern as the batch cell, so names with or without a\n",
    "suffix (e.g. `...ras_transect20_runup.nc`) are found. The old cell built the name as `...ras_transect20.nc`, so every\n",
    "transect was reported \"not found\" when the files carry `_runup`. Set `burst_id` to the part of the file name up to the\n",
    "camera (e.g. `1728124200.Sat.Oct.05_10_30_00.GMT.2024.CACO03.c1`), or leave it `None` to use the first burst in the\n",
    "folder. If the burst isn't there, the cell lists some that are.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How it works.** `xr.open_dataset` is *lazy*: it reads only the header until you ask for a variable, so pulling two 1-D\n",
    "arrays never loads the 1200 × 1181 × 3 image `I` (~4 MB per file) into memory. xarray also converts `_FillValue`s to NaN on read,\n",
